🌐 WEEK-8 FULL PRACTICAL GUIDE (BEGINNER FRIENDLY)

We’ll go in 3 parts:

SNS → Email
S3 → SNS → Email
S3 → SNS → SQS → Lambda (Full Architecture)
🔵 PART 1: SNS → EMAIL (STEP-BY-STEP)
👉 Step 0: Login
Go to: https://aws.amazon.com/console/
Login
✅ Step 1: Open SNS
Top search bar → type SNS
Click Amazon SNS
✅ Step 2: Create Topic

Left side menu:
👉 Click Topics

Top-right:
👉 Click Create topic

Now fill:

Type → Standard (radio button)
Name → MyEmailTopic

👉 Scroll down → Click Create topic

✅ Step 3: Create Email Subscription

After topic opens:

👉 Click Create subscription

Fill:

Protocol → dropdown → select Email
Endpoint → enter your email (e.g., harsha@gmail.com)

👉 Click Create subscription

✅ Step 4: Confirm Email

👉 Open your Gmail/Outlook
👉 Find email from AWS
👉 Click Confirm subscription

✔ Done

✅ Step 5: Send Test Message

Back to SNS topic:

👉 Click Publish message

Fill:

Subject → Test Mail
Message → Hello this is SNS test

👉 Click Publish message

📩 You will receive email

🟢 PART 2: S3 → SNS → EMAIL
✅ Step 1: Open S3

Search bar → type S3
Click Amazon S3

✅ Step 2: Create Bucket

👉 Click Create bucket

Fill:

Bucket name → my-upload-bucket-2026
Region → same as SNS (IMPORTANT)

Scroll down:

👉 Click Create bucket

✅ Step 3: Configure Event Notification

👉 Click your bucket name
👉 Click Properties tab

Scroll down:

👉 Find Event notifications

👉 Click Create event notification

Fill:

Event name → UploadNotification
Event types → tick ✔ All object create events

Destination:

Select → SNS topic
Choose → MyEmailTopic

👉 Click Save changes

✅ Step 4: Upload File (Test)

👉 Click Objects tab
👉 Click Upload

👉 Click Add files
👉 Select any file

👉 Click Upload

📩 You will receive email automatically

🟡 PART 3: S3 → SNS → SQS → LAMBDA

Now we build real architecture

🧱 Step 1: Create SQS Queue

Search → SQS
Click Amazon SQS

👉 Click Create queue

Fill:

Type → Standard
Name → MyS3Queue

👉 Click Create queue

🧱 Step 2: Create SNS Topic

Same like before:

Name → MyS3SNSTopic
🧱 Step 3: Subscribe SQS to SNS

👉 Open SNS topic
👉 Click Create subscription

Fill:

Protocol → Amazon SQS
Endpoint → select MyS3Queue

👉 Click Create subscription

🧱 Step 4: Set SQS Permission

👉 Open SQS → MyS3Queue
👉 Click Access policy
👉 Click Edit

👉 Paste policy (replace ARNs)

👉 Click Save

🧱 Step 5: Set SNS Permission for S3

👉 Open SNS topic
👉 Click Edit access policy

👉 Paste policy
👉 Click Save

🧱 Step 6: Connect S3 to SNS

👉 Open S3 bucket
👉 Go to Properties

👉 Event notifications → Create

Fill:

Event name → S3UploadEvent
Event type → ✔ All object create events
Destination → SNS topic → MyS3SNSTopic

👉 Click Save

🧱 Step 7: Check SQS Message

👉 Open SQS queue
👉 Click Send and receive messages

👉 Click Poll for messages

✔ You will see event message

🧱 Step 8: Create Lambda

Search → Lambda
Click AWS Lambda

👉 Click Create function

Fill:

Author from scratch
Function name → SQSConsumerFunction
Runtime → Python 3.x

👉 Click Create function

🧱 Step 9: Add Trigger

Inside Lambda:

👉 Click Add trigger

Select → SQS
Choose → MyS3Queue

👉 Click Add

🧱 Step 10: Add Code

Scroll to code editor:

Replace with:

def lambda_handler(event, context):
    for record in event['Records']:
        print("Message received from SQS:")
        print(record['body'])
    return {
        'statusCode': 200,
        'body': 'Message processed successfully'
    }

👉 Click Deploy

🧱 Step 11: Final Test

👉 Upload file to S3

Flow happens:

S3 → SNS → SQS → Lambda

👉 Go to Lambda
👉 Click Monitor tab
👉 Click View logs in CloudWatch

✔ You will see message printed

🎯 FINAL UNDERSTANDING (VERY IMPORTANT FOR EXAM)
Amazon S3 → Stores files
Amazon SNS → Sends notifications
Amazon SQS → Stores messages safely
AWS Lambda → Processes automatically
